course: dictionary
lesson: 10389
title: Trestle: a frame that holds things up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A trestle is a frame with legs, often a beam on two pairs of sloping legs, that holds up a table top or a plank. Read the words around the word first. In «a long table on trestles», the table is the thing being held up, so a trestle must be the support underneath it.
explain: The kitchen sentence gives you a clue for another word too: «two high-backed settles (settle = a long wooden bench with a high back)». The brackets explain the word, so you do not have to guess. Brackets, commas and dashes can all carry clues.
explain: Trestle can mean more than one thing. At school fairs and harvest suppers, food is laid on trestle tables that fold away easily. A trestle can also be the framework of beams that holds up a railway bridge. To check, swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A trestle is a frame with legs, often a beam on two pairs of sloping legs.
fact: A trestle table is a long table made of a board on trestles, and it is easy to fold away.
fact: «Settle» means a long wooden bench with a high back.
fact: A trestle is also a framework of beams that holds up a railway bridge, especially in North America.
fact: Trestle tables appear in The Wind in the Willows, where a feast is laid out on them.
exercise: «The kitchen has a long table on trestles.» What is a trestle here? | A type of chimney | *A frame with legs that holds up a table top | A hanging herb | A kind of wooden bench with a high back
exercise: Find and copy one word from the kitchen sentence that means a long wooden bench with a high back. | rafters | *settles | hams | herbs
exercise: «A trestle bridge carries a railway across a valley.» What holds the railway up? | *A framework of beams | A stone wall | The valley | A train
test: At a school fair, why is food often laid on trestle tables? | Because trestles are very tall and can reach the ceiling | Because trestles are made of food | Because a trestle is a kind of bench | *Because the tables are easy to fold away
test: Which of these is a trestle? | A kind of railway train | *A frame with two pairs of sloping legs holding up a beam | A hanging herb in a kitchen | A long wooden bench with a high back
exam: In «a long table on trestles», which word tells you the trestles are what the table rests on? | long | kitchen | *on | table
